Z||000000||Beaverman||08-18-2001||08:15 PM||||Well I get off of work the other day and i'm beginning my 30 minute drive home and all was well until i get on the interstate and then Blah says my car and loses all power.  Then as i pull off an offramp it starts to sputter and kinda kick. It starts fine but when it gear its like blah i don't want to go fast without cutting out.  Any ideas wut the problem is?  I was thinking an o2 sensor but i don't know.  Car is an 87 2.8.  Check engine light comes on as it sputters and or dies.<P>Thanks<p>[This message has been edited by Beaverman (edited 08-18-2001).]||||reg||9
Z||000001||Fiero_24||08-18-2001||08:26 PM||||Change the ignition module.  I just posted 2-3 weeks ago on this same problem.  Let me guess, you can drive for a short while and then 100RPM and a big bang, right?  Mine was running really bad until it finally went out.  They only run about $24 at autozone.  They will test the old one, but if it is heat related (Like mine was) the test will say it is fine since it is not in a hot engine compartment.<P>Craig<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24</A> <BR>1987 GT||||reg||1
